> to own and<strong> </strong>scale end-to-end employee lifecycle operations for a large, distributed, feet-on-street workforce with high monthly churn, ensuring accuracy, speed, compliance, and cost efficiency. The role is critical in enabling uninterrupted business operations through robust onboarding, offboarding, payroll and statutory compliance, particularly in a piece-rate compensation environment.</p>\n<p><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong> Employee Lifecycle Management</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li>Own and continuously improve end-to-end lifecycle processes, including:</li>\n<ul>\n<li>Offer issuance and acceptance at scale</li>\n<li>Bulk onboarding and induction readiness</li>\n<li>Background verification (BGV) initiation, tracking, and closure</li>\n<li>Data integrity across HRMS, payroll, and compliance systems</li>\n<li>Exit processing, final settlements, and statutory closures</li>\n</ul>\n<li>Ensure lifecycle SLAs are met despite high daily transaction volumes.</li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li><strong> High-Volume Onboarding &amp; Workforce Readiness</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li>Design and operate bulk hiring and onboarding models capable of handling ~1,000 joiners per week.</li>\n<li>Ensure seamless coordination between recruitment, business HR, HRMS, payroll, and compliance teams</li>\n<li>Drive standardisation of documentation and exception handling for ensuring deployment-readiness from Day 1</li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li><strong> FTC Management&nbsp;</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li>Own the entire lifecycle processes for the fixed-term contract employees on third party payroll.</li>\n<li>Guide the team for timely payroll and F&amp;F process for disbursements and the required vendor compliances.</li>\n<li>Oversee process alignment, adherence and exception management with Business HR team, Finance team and Compliance team.</li>\n<li>Review of the vendor (third party payroll provider) and their performance evaluation on process and compliance adherence.</li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li><strong> Statutory Compliance &amp; Remittances</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li>Ensure full compliance across central and state labour laws, including&nbsp;</li>\n<ul>\n<li>Registrations and remittances for EPF, ESI, PT, LWF</li>\n<li>Adherence to the Minimum Wages (time-rate floors in piece-rate scenarios)</li>\n<li>CLRA (in cases of third party roll employees) and state-specific registrations</li>\n<li>Timely statutory filings, challans, and remittances</li>\n</ul>\n<li>Own audit readiness for internal, statutory, and external audits.</li>\n<ul>\n<li>Partner closely with Legal, Finance, and Internal Audit for supporting the audit processes</li>\n</ul>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li><strong> Vendor &amp; Partner Management</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li>Manage multiple vendors across:</li>\n<ul>\n<li>Payroll processing</li>\n<li>Background verification</li>\n<li>Compliance filings</li>\n</ul>\n<li>Define clear SLAs, KPIs, and penalty structures for meeting timelines and quality</li>\n<li>Drive cost optimisation without compromising compliance or employee experience</li>\n<li>Ensure vendor scalability aligns with business growth and churn dynamics</li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li><strong> Technology &amp; Process Excellence</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li>Leverage HRMS, payroll systems, attendance/productivity tools, and automation</li>\n<li>Drive digitisation and straight-through processing wherever possible</li>\n<li>Continuously improve TATs, reduce manual effort, and enhance scalability</li>\n<li>Ensure systems can handle extreme transaction volumes without failure</li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li><strong> Process Leadership and Team Management</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li>Provide in-depth guidance to the team, fostering a culture of continuous improvement and functional expertise.</li>\n<li>Act as a functional expert within HR Operations, bringing deep expertise and a point of view on the broader business landscape.</li>\n<li>Lead a multi-layered operations team and fostering a culture of rigor, ownership, and continuous improvement</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Key Qualifications &amp; Experience</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>12+ years of progressive experience in HR Operations, Shared Services, or Payroll Management with a proven track record of handling high-volume, blue-collar, or salesforce (preferably 15,000+ headcount).</li>\n<li>Deep functional expertise in managing the full employee lifecycle and high-stakes statutory compliance (registrations, remittances) in India.</li>\n<li>Proven experience in designing and executing scalable, automated solutions for payroll and BGV in a high-attrition environment.</li>\n<li>Strong problem-solving and exception-handling capability</li>\n<li>Data-driven decision making</li>\n<li>MBA / PG Diploma in HR or equivalent is preferred.</li>\n<li>High proficiency in MS Excel</li>\n</ul><div class=\"content-conclusion\"><p><strong>PhonePe Full Time Employee Benefits (Not applicable for Intern or Contract Roles)</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Insurance Benefits - </strong>Medical Insurance, Critical Illness Insurance, Accidental Insurance, Life Insurance</li>\n<li><strong>Wellness Program -</strong> Employee Assistance Program, Onsite Medical Center, Emergency Support System</li>\n<li><strong>Parental Support - </strong>Maternity Benefit, Paternity Benefit Program, Adoption Assistance Program, Day-care Support Program</li>\n<li><strong>Mobility Benefits - </strong>Relocation benefits, Transfer Support Policy, Travel Policy</li>\n<li><strong>Retirement Benefits - </strong>Employee PF Contribution, Flexible PF Contribution, Gratuity, NPS, Leave Encashment&nbsp;</li>\n<li><strong>Other Benefits - </strong>Higher Education Assistance, Car Lease, Salary Advance Policy</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong><em>Our inclusive culture promotes individual expression, creativity, innovation, and achievement and in turn helps us better understand and serve our customers. We see ourselves as a place