n who ensures they do. Your job is to take the core hook of a video and turn it into a high-impact visual that stands out in a crowded feed. You will work in an AI-first environment, using generative tools to create assets and variations that would take hours to build by hand.</p>\n<p><strong>Focus Area 1: Visual Storytelling and CTR Optimization</strong>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>You own the \"click.\"</p>\n<ul>\n<li>You design thumbnails that tell a story in a split second. You understand how to use composition, contrast, and color theory to guide the viewer\u2019s eye exactly where you want it.</li>\n<li>You are a master of \"The Hook.\" You know how to pair a compelling image with minimal text to create curiosity or urgency.</li>\n<li>You manage facial expressions and emotive triggers. You know how to select or generate the perfect \"hero\" image that connects with a human audience.</li>\n<li>You work closely with the Channel Intelligence Lead to analyze A/B test results and refine your designs based on actual performance data.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Focus Area 2: AI-First Composition and Workflow</strong>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>You use the machine to outpace the competition.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>You are a power user of generative AI tools like Midjourney, DALL-E 3, or Stable Diffusion to create unique assets, backgrounds, and characters from scratch.</li>\n<li>You use the latest AI features in Photoshop (like Generative Fill and Expand) to manipulate images, swap elements, and clean up compositions in seconds.</li>\n<li>You build and maintain a library of AI-generated assets that allow us to move from a concept to a finished thumbnail in record time.</li>\n<li>You stay ahead of the curve. When a new AI model or technique drops that can improve our visual quality or speed, you are the first to master it.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Focus Area 3: Iteration and Data-Driven Design</strong>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>You don't just make one version; you build a system for winning.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>You produce multiple variations for every video. You understand that the first idea isn't always the best, and you use AI to quickly test different angles, colors, and compositions.</li>\n<li>You are obsessed with the \"why\" behind the click. You look at CTR (Click-Through Rate) data and qualified view metrics to understand which visual styles are resonating with our specific audience.</li>\n<li>You ensure brand consistency. While every thumbnail is an experiment, you make sure the overall \"look\" of the channel remains premium and recognizable.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>What We Are Looking For</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Technical Agility:</strong> You are a master of the Adobe Suite and a power user of generative AI. You don't get hung up on tools; you use whatever gets the best result the fastest.</li>\n<li><strong>Attention to Detail:</strong> You have an eye for lighting, shadows, and perspective. You ensure that AI-generated elements blend perfectly into the final composition so they never look \"fake.\"</li>\n<li><strong>Speed without sacrificing quality:</strong> You thrive on high-volume output. You can turn around multiple high-end thumbnails in a single day without the quality ever dipping.</li>\n<li><strong>Analytical Thinking:</strong> You don't just \"feel\" that a design is good. You look at the data and can explain why a certain visual is likely to perform better.</li>\n<li><strong>High Ownership:</strong> You treat the CTR of every video as your personal responsibility. If a video is underperforming, you are already building a new thumbnail before anyone asks.</li>\n</ul><div class=\"content-conclusion\"><p><strong>PhonePe Full Time Employee Benefits (Not applicable for Intern or Contract Roles)</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Insurance Benefits - </strong>Medical Insurance, Critical Illness Insurance, Accidental Insurance, Life Insurance</li>\n<li><strong>Wellness Program -</strong> Employee Assistance Program, Onsite Medical Center, Emergency Support Syst