ity to navigate diverse business practices across multiple countries.</p>\n<h3 style=\"line-height: 1;\"><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h3>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"line-height: 1;\">Drive sales for Druva\u2019s Endpoints and data protection solutions across assigned accounts in UK, EMEA and ROW.<br><br></li>\n<li style=\"line-height: 1;\">Consistently achieve or exceed annual revenue targets through a mix of new customer acquisition and existing account growth.<br><br></li>\n<li style=\"line-height: 1;\">Engage and influence C-level executives, IT leadership, and procurement teams in diverse industry sectors.<br><br></li>\n<li style=\"line-height: 1;\">Manage complex sales cycles that often involve multiple countries, stakeholders, and decision-making processes.<br><br></li>\n<li style=\"line-height: 1;\">Build and maintain trusted relationships with international channel partners, distributors, and systems integrators.<br><br></li>\n<li style=\"line-height: 1;\">Deliver compelling, localised solution demonstrations both virtually and onsite.<br><br></li>\n<li style=\"line-height: 1;\">Maintain awareness of data protection regulations (including GDPR) and regional compliance considerations.<br><br></li>\n<li style=\"line-height: 1;\">Contribute to a collaborative, customer-first culture within Druva\u2019s international sales team.<br><br></li>\n<li style=\"line-height: 1;\">Travel as required (up to 25%) for customer meetings, events, and partner engagements.<br><br></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 style=\"line-height: 1;\"><strong>What Makes You a Great Fit</strong></h3>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"line-height: 1;\">Demonstrated success selling into enterprise and/or commercial organisations across multiple EMEA/UK/ROW markets.<br><br></li>\n<li style=\"line-height: 1;\">Proven experience in cloud, backup/recovery, cybersecurity, or infrastructure SaaS solutions.<br><br></li>\n<li style=\"line-height: 1;\">Strong track record of exceeding quota in high-growth, competitive markets.<br><br></