es.</li>\n<li>Develop and continuously improve commercial agreement templates, playbooks, policies and legal processes to drive consistency, efficiency and scalability across the commercial legal function.</li>\n<li>Evaluate and leverage AI-enabled legal technologies and workflows to improve contracting efficiency, enhance legal operations, support data-driven decision-making and enable the commercial legal team to scale while maintaining high-quality legal work.</li>\n<li>Build strong relationships across the company and foster a practical, collaborative and business-oriented approach to legal partnership</li>\n</ul>\n<h3><strong>What Makes You a Great Fit:</strong></h3>\n<ul>\n<li>JD or equivalent U.S. law degree and active bar membership in good standing in at least one U.S. jurisdiction.</li>\n<li>10+ years of commercial legal experience supporting technology companies in the SaaS industry with demonstrated experience leading complex, high-value enterprise technology transactions, including negotiations with Fortune 500 and other large enterprise customers.</li>\n<li>Demonstrated experience managing, mentoring and developing attorneys.</li>\n<li>Exceptional judgment with the ability to balance legal risk and business objectives in a fast-paced, high-growth environment.</li>\n<li>Proven ability to build trusted relationships with senior business stakeholders and provide practical, business-oriented legal advice.</li>\n<li>Significant experience with data protection and privacy laws (including GDPR and CCPA), information security terms and technology contracting.</li>\n<li>Outstanding drafting, negotiation, communication, and interpersonal skills.</li>\n<li>Proven ability to independently manage numerous complex, business-critical matters and competing priorities.</li>\n<li>Demonstrated ability to improve legal processes, develop scalable contracting resources and drive operational excellence.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bonus Points For:&nbsp;</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Recognition fr