      "description": "<div class=\"content-intro\"><p>Elastic, the Search AI Company, enables everyone to find the answers they need in real time, using all their data, at scale \u2014 unleashing the potential of businesses and people. The Elastic Search AI Platform, used by more than 50% of the Fortune 500, brings together the precision of search and the intelligence of AI to enable everyone to accelerate the results that matter. By taking advantage of all structured and unstructured data \u2014 securing and protecting private information more effectively \u2014 Elastic\u2019s complete, cloud-based solutions for search, security, and observability help organizations deliver on the promise of AI.</p></div><h2 class=\"public-DraftStyleDefault-block public-DraftStyleDefault-ltr\" data-offset-key=\"bb4ua-0-0\"><span data-offset-key=\"bb4ua-0-0\"><span data-text=\"true\">What is the role? </span></span></h2>\n<div class=\"public-DraftStyleDefault-block public-DraftStyleDefault-ltr\" data-offset-key=\"bb4ua-0-0\"><span data-offset-key=\"bb4ua-0-0\"><span data-text=\"true\">The role will be tasked with developing and maintaining our Application Hosting Infrastructure on Kubernetes in GCP. </span></span><span data-offset-key=\"72duc-0-0\"><span data-text=\"true\">As a Platform Engineer, you will play a critical role in developing and maintaining our core application infrastructure that supports our business operations. You\u2019ll be part of a small, focused team that prioritizes automation and security while engineering a robust platform for hosting internal applications. This position offers the chance to work with the latest technologies in an AI-forward environment, allowing you to contribute to impactful projects that drive our growth.</span></span></div>\n<h2 class=\"public-DraftStyleDefault-block public-DraftStyleDefault-ltr\" data-offset-key=\"7c920-0-0\"><span data-offset-key=\"7c920-0-0\"><span data-text=\"true\">What You Will Be Doing</span></span></h2>\n<ul cla