gainst territory targets (the headline metric); execution of the partner sales playbooks that grow average deal size; committed and reviewed Technical Engagement Plans; and published repeatable assets. Pipeline and capacity, not activity.</p>\n<h2><strong>What you bring</strong></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Fluency in French, Spanish, and English (business level) is a mandatory requirement</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Experience in at least one of those technologies/solutions is a must: enterprise search, observability, or cybersecurity</strong></li>\n<li>Experience with cybersecurity (SIEM, SOAR, XDR, Endpoint) is a strong advantage</li>\n<li>5+ years in technology solutions, practice development, architecture, consulting and/or cloud/infrastructure technologies.</li>\n<li>5+ years of pre-sales experience in the software sector, ideally partner-facing: channel, alliances, SI/GSI or MSSP ecosystems.</li>\n<li>A one-to-many mindset: you would rather teach ten engineers to run the demo than run it ten times yourself, and you can show where your enablement turned into someone else's win.</li>\n<li>Working knowledge of security operations (SIEM, endpoint, cloud security) and/or observability \u2014 the solution areas where our partner business is growing fastest \u2014 plus an understanding of AI and semantic search technologies (RAG, vector search, NLP).</li>\n<li>Professional experience architecting or operating solutions on AWS, Google Cloud or Microsoft Azure.</li>\n<li>Commercial fluency: you can read a deal, talk services scope and margin with a partner, and translate technical capability into the business case their customer buys.</li>\n<li>Excellent communication and presentation skills for technical and non-technical audiences \u2014 a partner engineer in the morning, an architect in the afternoon, an executive sponsor in the evening.</li>\n<li>Comfort with ambiguity and a self-starter's bias to action; you inspire partner teams to work on what is most relevant, not just what is urgent.</li>\n<li>Ability to travel up to 30%.</li>\n</ul><div class=\"content-pay-transparency\"><div class=\"pay-input\"><div class=\"description\"><p>Compensation for this role is in the form of base salary plus a variable component.</p>\n<p>At Elastic, our compensation philosophy aims to provide fair, competitive and transparent remuneration. Salary ranges are established based on a combination of external market benchmarks, internal pay equity considerations, and the responsibilities and complexity associated with each role. This approach helps ensure consistency across comparable roles while remaining competitive within the relevant labour markets.</p>\n<p>The final compensation offered within the applicable range will be determined based on several objective factors, including relevant professional experience, level of skills and expertise, alignment with the role requirements, and the overall scope and complexity of the position.</p></div><div class=\"title\">The typical starting On-Target Earnings range (Base Salary + Variable) for this role is:</div><div class=\"pay-range\"><span>\u20ac104.800</span><span class=\"divider\">&mdash;</span><span>\u20ac165.800 EUR</span></div></div></div><div class=\"content-conclusion\"><h2><strong>Additional Information - We Take Care of Our People</strong></h2>\n<p>As a distributed company, diversity drives our identity. Whether you\u2019re looking to launch a new career or grow an existing one, Elastic is the type of company where you can balance great work with great life. Your age is only a number. It doesn\u2019t matter if you\u2019re just out of college or your children are; we need you for what you can do.</p>\n<p>We strive to have parity of benefits across regions and while regulations differ from place to place, we believe taking care of our people is the right thing to do.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Competitive pay based on the work you do here and not your previous salary</li>\n<li>Health coverage for you and your