ology landscape.</li>\n<li><strong>Lead global public sector communications. </strong>Oversee our strategic public sector communications program, including engagement with government, public sector technology, and policy-relevant audiences in priority markets.</li>\n<li><strong>Modernize the external communications operating model.</strong> Build an organization designed for the AI era. Determine where human expertise and judgment create differentiated value, where AI and automation can increase speed and scale, and where agencies provide specialist capability or market leverage. Eliminate low-value activity rather than simply making it more efficient.</li>\n<li><strong>Build an intelligence-led function.</strong> Use media intelligence, competitive signals, analyst insight, social listening, audience data, and performance measurement to understand what is landing, where perceptions are shifting, and where Elastic should act. Feed those insights back into the broader story and communications planning process.</li>\n<li><strong>Lead the global external communications team and agency ecosystem.</strong> Build and develop a high-performing team of specialist communications leaders. Establish clear accountability, raise the standard of strategic and technical communications thinking, and ensure agencies operate as extensions of Elastic's strategy rather than independent engines of activity.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>What You Bring</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Significant senior leadership experience in external or corporate communications within enterprise technology, cloud, infrastructure, cybersecurity, data, developer platforms, or AI.</li>\n<li>Strong technical fluency and genuine curiosity about technology. You don't need to be an engineer, but you must be comfortable engaging deeply with Product and Engineering leaders and understanding sophisticated technical concepts.</li>\n<li>A demonstrated ability to take highly technical products, capabilities, and developer stories and find the larger story that matters to our technical audience of CIOs, CISOs, CTOs, IT leaders, and the market.</li>\n<li>Experience leading specialist technology communications teams and enabling subject-matter experts to operate effectively with Product, PMM, Engineering, and senior business leaders.</li>\n<li>Demonstrated experience building and leading a sophisticated global external communications function rather than simply managing media relations.</li>\n<li>Strong understanding of developer and practitioner audiences alongside technical enterprise technology decision-makers and the important differences in what earns credibility with each.</li>\n<li>Excellent editorial judgment, with the ability to recognize the genuinely interesting story inside complex technology and the confidence to reject activity that isn't likely to create meaningful impact.</li>\n<li>Deep understanding of how reputation and market perception are built through earned media, technical communities, speaking, podcasts, executives, customers, partners, analysts, social channels, and other credible third parties.</li>\n<li>Strong relationships with influential business and technology media.</li>\n<li>Experience leading global and regional teams and managing complex agency ecosystems.</li>\n<li>A data- and intelligence-led approach to communications strategy and measurement.</li>\n<li>A track record of using AI, technology, automation, and new operating approaches to increase communications effectiveness and productivity.</li>\n<li>The ability to operate comfortably with senior executives, challenge constructively, make decisions with incomplete information, and bring clarity when priorities are moving quickly.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>#LI-JM5</p><div class=\"content-pay-transparency\"><div class=\"pay-input\"><div class=\"description\"><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br>Compensation for this role is in the form of base salary.&nbsp; This role does not have a variable compensation compone