ect attendance, designing pre-/post-event nurture tracks, and ensuring rigorous pipeline follow-up.</li>\n<li>Targeting &amp; Segmentation: Partner with SDRs and Sales to identify high-priority target accounts and build highly segmented lists based on market priorities.</li>\n<li>Content &amp; Messaging: Map, plan, and create compelling messages and creative tailored to prioritized accounts and specific event touch-points.</li>\n<li>Digital Collaboration: Collaborate closely with the Digital Marketing Manager to create effective media strategies that surround target accounts.</li>\n<li>Campaign Execution: Build and run regional email programs, direct marketing efforts, and optimized landing pages to convert interest into sales-accepted opportunities.</li>\n<li>Global Alignment: Work closely with the Global Acquisition Marketing team to implement and scale localized strategies.</li>\n<li>Analytics &amp; Optimization: Leverage analytics tools to measure and determine the effectiveness of campaigns and event activations across all touch points.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Who You Are</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>3+ years of experience in a B2B demand generation or integrated marketing role, with a proven track record of driving net-new customer acquisition.</li>\n<li>5+ years of experience in marketing or similar</li>\n<li>Proficiency with ABM and marketing automation tools; knowledge of Marketo is a strong plus.</li>\n<li>Analytical mindset with experience using data to optimize campaigns. Experience with Looker (or similar BI tools) is a plus.</li>\n<li>A healthy balance between strategic thinking and hands-on execution\u2014you can design the plan and build it, too.</li>\n<li>Agile &amp; Self-Motivated: A self-starting contributor with the ability to multitask, prioritize responsibilities, and navigate a fast-paced environment.</li>\n<li>Native spoken and written Swedish is required.</li>\n<li>Fluent spoken and written English is required.</li>\n<li>Travel: Willingness and a