      "description": "<p><strong>This is Adyen</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Adyen provides payments, data, and financial products in a single solution for customers like Meta, Uber, H&amp;M, and Microsoft - making us the financial technology platform of choice. At Adyen, everything we do is engineered for ambition.&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">For our teams, we create an environment with opportunities for our people to succeed, backed by the culture and support to ensure they are enabled to truly own their careers. We are motivated individuals who tackle unique technical challenges at scale and solve them as a team. Together, we deliver innovative and ethical solutions that help businesses achieve their ambitions faster.</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<h3><strong>Engineering Manager, Capital</strong><strong><br><br></strong></h3>\n<p><strong>The Opportunity&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p>We\u2019re looking for an Engineering Manager to lead the development of our Capital product, powering how businesses conduct business expenses and payment transactions. Capital is the next growth frontier as Adyen grows into a comprehensive financial service provider beyond Payments. <br><br>This is a rapidly growing space, giving you the opportunity to influence the strategy, own the roadmap, explore and deploy AI first product development, and see it through from early build to a scaled product.</p>\n<p>As an engineering leader, you\u2019ll work closely with partners across engineering, product, commercial, and operations to deliver a best-in-class Issuing solution that serves both enterprise clients and embedded finance partners. This San Francisco-based role is part of the broader Financial Products organization, which owns the full suite of financial services at Adyen.</p>\n<p><strong>What You'll Do:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Drive the Roadmap:</strong> Develop and execute the technical roadmap for expanding the richness of our Issuing