rategy</li>\n<li>Security and compliance readiness across device software, release and certification flows</li>\n<li>Tools and processes that make launches safer, more predictable and easier to scale</li>\n<li>This is not a ticket-management role. It is not a pure delivery role. You will define the product direction for a broad, engineering-heavy platform area: understanding the teams that depend on these capabilities, setting clear priorities, defining success metrics and connecting the work to broader Payments and business outcomes.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>What you'll do:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Define the product vision and roadmap for the platform capabilities that support fleet stability, testing, release, observability, certification and security readiness.</li>\n<li>Partner with Product and Engineering leadership to build a broader vision for device fleet stability and reliability across In-Person Payments.</li>\n<li>Turn a broad engineering-led area into a clear product area with users, outcomes, priorities, trade-offs and measurable impact.</li>\n<li>Own the product direction for testing infrastructure, including emulators, robot testing and hardware-in-the-loop setups.</li>\n<li>Provide tools built around the needs of the teams that use them, by understanding their workflows, pain points and release risks.</li>\n<li>Own the product direction for release and rollout infrastructure, including staged rollouts, automated release signals and rollback tooling.</li>\n<li>Make release processes across our fleet of devices safer, more automated and more predictable.</li>\n<li>Drive the product direction for monitoring and fleet health insights: the data and tooling that help teams understand device and payment application health, detect issues early and act before merchants are impacted.</li>\n<li>Shape the approach to continuous pre-certification tooling, capacity and strategy, so certification becomes a final validation step rather than a place where issues are found late.</li>\n<li>Collaborate with Security, Certifications, Engineering, Product and vendor-facing teams to embed quality, compliance and release readiness earlier in the lifecycle.</li>\n<li>Define clear metrics for product stability, launch quality, release confidence and adoption of the platform capabilities you own.</li>\n<li>Ensure the roadmap is tied to clear business outcomes and aligned with the broader Payments and company strategy.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Who you are:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Knowledge - You have a strong understanding of software delivery, testing, observability and release processes.</li>\n<li>Experience with technical platforms, infrastructure, developer tooling, reliability products or device platforms is a strong plus.</li>\n<li>Mindset - You are a self-starter who can create structure in an ambiguous environment and build product management for a technical area from the ground up.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Our Diversity, Equity and Inclusion commitments&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Our unique approach is a product of our diverse perspectives. This diversity of backgrounds and cultures is essential in helping us maintain our momentum. Our business and technical challenges are unique, and we need as many different voices as possible to join us in solving them - voices like yours. No matter who you are or where you\u2019re from, we welcome you to be your true self at Adyen.&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Studies show that women and members of underrepresented communities apply for jobs only if they meet 100% of the qualifications. Does this sound like you? If so, Adyen encourages you to reconsider and apply. We look forward to your application!</span></p>\n<p><strong>What\u2019s next?</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Ensuring a smooth and enjoyable candidate experience is critical for us. We aim to get back to you regarding your application within 5 business days. Ou