      "description": "<p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>This is Adyen</strong></span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-size: 12pt;\">Adyen provides payments, data, and financial products in a single solution for customers like Meta, Uber, H&amp;M, and Microsoft - making us the financial technology platform of choice. At Adyen, everything we do is engineered for ambition.&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-size: 12pt;\">For our teams, we create an environment with opportunities for our people to succeed, backed by the culture and support to ensure they are enabled to truly own their careers. We are motivated individuals who tackle unique technical challenges at scale and solve them as a team. Together, we deliver innovative and ethical solutions that help businesses achieve their ambitions faster.</span></p>\n<h1><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>About the team and the role</strong></span></h1>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Platform Engineering enables business growth by providing the shared foundation that lets Adyen engineers autonomously build and support secure, scalable, and reliable products \u2014 from data centers and networks to deployment environments and database solutions.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">As Senior Service Designer for Platform Engineering, you will improve the end-to-end developer experience across internal tools, workflows, and platform capabilities. The role blends service design, UX strategy, and hands-on design consultancy. You will act as the bridge between high-level strategy and tactical execution, making Platform Engineering feel and function like a single, cohesive experience rather than ~100 disconnected products.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">You will start with the Developer Center \u2014 the central developer platform and launch pad for everything else \u2014 then expand to the journey across the wider developer ecosystem, which today is fragmented and inconsistent. You will work on both improving what exists and shaping what comes next.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">You can expect an 80/20 split as you come into Adyen, where 80% of your time and work will be in service design, and 20% could involve hands-on user experience or user interface design. At Adyen, people own their career, so while this is what you can expect initially, this role will be yours to shape.</span></p>\n<h1><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Why this role</strong></span></h1>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; <strong>Greenfield by design. </strong>Service design as a coordinated practice does not yet exist at Adyen. You are not inheriting a playbook \u2014 you are writing it, and socializing it across PX as the example of what good looks like.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; <strong>Real scope, real impact. </strong>Your users are ~1,500 engineers. The frictions you remove and the journeys you connect translate directly into how fast Adyen can build and ship.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; <strong>A seat where decisions are made. </strong>You will influence and co-create roadmaps and priorities with engineering and product leadership \u2014 not just respond to them.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; <strong>Room to grow the craft. </strong>You will teach and share service design across the PX practice, helping other designers adopt these methods and creating a multiplier effect well beyond your own projects.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h1><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>What you\u2019ll do</strong></span></h1>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>Build the service ecosystem. </strong>Map and own the end-to-end service journey for Platform Engineering. You look beyond the screen to design how people, processes, and technology work together to create a seamless experience.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>Drive continuous improvement across systems. </strong>Create interventions that change how whole teams and systems work together, advancing the organization \u2014 not just individual features.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>Enable design thinking at scale. </strong>Act as a consultant to product and engineering teams, giving them the tools and methodologies to apply design to their own problem spaces.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>Shape AI-enabled developer experiences. </strong>Design how AI shows up in developer workflows \u2014 from discovery and self-service to troubleshooting, documentation, and automation \u2014 applying it where it creates real value and improves productivity without adding complexity.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>Define the strategic vision. </strong>Take ownership of broad, undefined spaces within the internal developer platform. You frame the problem and create a clear service strategy that balances user needs with technical and regulatory constraints.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>Consult on UX/UI excellence. </strong>Partner with product teams to ensure individual features align with the broader platform logic and meet our high bar for usability. Should be comfortable solving or unblocking UI or UX problems as they arise in teams.&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>Partner across the organization. </strong>Work with Product, Technology, and Data Analytics to turn complex data into actionable service blueprints and long-term roadmaps.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>Articulate value. </strong>Communicate service methodologies and the tangible business impact they deliver to senior stakeholders and cross-functional partners.</span></p>\n<h1><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>This is you</strong></span></h1>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>Experience. </strong>8+ years in design overall, including 3+ years specifically in service design, navigating complex software or hardware environments. You have a proven track record of using service design to simplify intricate workflows in SaaS or B2B products.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>Full-stack service design. </strong>You develop a deep, top-to-bottom understanding of the systems underlying developer touchpoints, so you can make operational improvements that matter to people and have a positive impact on developer satisfaction and retention.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>Systems thinking. </strong>You see the big picture. You map intricate journeys that span entire ecosystems \u2014 looking up, down, and across \u2014 ensuring consistency and logic at every touchpoint.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>Consulting mindset. </strong>You are comfortable as a coach and advisor, empowering other teams to make design-led decisions while holding a high bar for the final output.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>Exceptional communication. </strong>Standout facilitation and storytelling skills. You think about both company systems and people systems, and you build alignment across teams that don\u2019t naturally work together.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>Technically fluent. </strong>Strongly tech-savvy and comfortable in technical conversations without needing to be an engineer. Ideally you\u2019ve built complex application offerings or worked as a systems designer in an ecosystem environment.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>AI and innovation mindset.</strong> You have experience integrating AI tools into the end-to-end design process \u2014 leveraging AI for research, synthesis, or prototyping \u2014 and you can enable others to use these tools to work smarter and faster.&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Nice to have</strong></span></p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; Familiarity with business banking, fintech, or enterprise financial services, and comfort with data-heavy surfaces and complex financial user needs.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; International work experience.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>Our Diversity, Equity and Inclusion commitments&nbsp;</strong></span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-size: 12pt;\">Our unique approach is a product of our diverse perspectives. This diversity of backgrounds and cultures is essential in helping us maintain our momentum. Our business and technical challenges are unique, and we need as many different voices as possible to join us in solving them - voices like yours. No matter who you are or where you\u2019re from, we welcome you to be your true self at Adyen.&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-size: 12pt;\">Studies show that women and members of underrepresented communities apply for jobs only if they meet 100% of the qualifications. Does this sound like you? If so, Adyen encourages you to reconsider and apply. We look forward to your application!</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>What\u2019s next?</strong></span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Ensuring a smooth and enjoyable candidate experience is critical for us. We aim to get back to you regarding your application within 5 business days. Our interview process tends to take about 4 weeks to complete, but may fluctuate depending on the role. </span><a href=\"https://careers.adyen.com/how-we-hire\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Learn more about our hiring process here</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. Don\u2019t be afraid to let us know if you need more flexibility.</span></span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">This role is based out of our Amsterdam office. We are an office-first company and value in-person collaboration; we do not offer remote-only roles.</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
