      "description": "<p><strong>This is Adyen</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Adyen provides payments, data, and financial products in a single solution for customers like Meta, Uber, H&amp;M, and Microsoft - making us the financial technology platform of choice. At Adyen, everything we do is engineered for ambition.&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">For our teams, we create an environment with opportunities for our people to succeed, backed by the culture and support to ensure they are enabled to truly own their careers. We are motivated individuals who tackle unique technical challenges at scale and solve them as a team. Together, we deliver innovative and ethical solutions that help businesses achieve their ambitions faster.</span></p>\n<p><strong>About the role: purpose &amp; impact</strong></p>\n<p>As the Tooling Manager in the Professional Services Excellence team, you own the tools and systems that PS runs on. You decide what we build, what we buy, and what we retire, and then you make it real. Your work shows up as workflows that run themselves, data that leadership can act on, and delivery teams that spend less time working around their tooling and more time with customers.</p>\n<p>This is a build role, not an administration one. You are hands-on: you architect and deploy automation and AI-driven workflows rather than maintaining platforms that someone else selected. This is also a founding role on a new team, so you will help shape how the function operates and where it focuses first, not step into a fixed playbook. You will be the first dedicated owner of tooling in PS, which means the remit is yours to define together with the team.</p>\n<p>Your scope is global. The systems you own are used by delivery teams in every region and touch every merchant we onboard, so you will work with leaders and team members across regions and influence stakeholders across time zones. Your impact will show up in faster onboarding, c