insight that PS leadership can act on.</li>\n<li>Measure whether tools are genuinely used and used well, and act on what that tells you about where the real friction sits.</li>\n<li>Distill complex system dependencies into simple explanations for non-technical stakeholders, and partner with enablement and knowledge owners so documentation and playbooks stay accurate.</li>\n<li>Set and hold the standards for data quality, security, and compliance across the tools and automated workflows you own.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Who you are</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>You bring senior-level judgment and presence, with around 7 to 10 years in technical operations, systems or revenue operations, and a track record of scaling delivery infrastructure in a fast-growing environment.</li>\n<li>You are a hands-on builder. You are comfortable with APIs, webhooks, JSON, and relational data structures, and you have used agentic tools and AI coding assistants to ship solutions that people actually use.</li>\n<li>You have advanced configuration and administration skills across modern project management tools, enterprise collaboration suites, and automation platforms, with a strong grasp of data flows and integration dependencies.</li>\n<li>You think in systems, weighing the downstream effects of a configuration choice on data integrity and on how the landscape scales.</li>\n<li>You make high-conviction decisions with incomplete information, and you deploy, test, and iterate quickly rather than waiting for certainty.</li>\n<li>You have a strong sense of ownership. You take accountability when something you own breaks, you are honest about it, and you fix the root cause.</li>\n<li>You translate operational needs into clean system logic, and you explain technical concepts to non-technical audiences without losing them or oversimplifying.</li>\n<li>You enjoy working with a wide range of stakeholders, prioritizing competing requests, managing change, and driving adoption of new ways of working.</li