cipate what is needed, maintain command of competing priorities, and follow through without repeated reminders.</li>\n<li><strong>Resourceful and polished.</strong> You operate confidently with senior and high-profile stakeholders while remaining humble enough to manage the smallest details.</li>\n<li><strong>Calm under pressure.</strong> You remain composed and solution-oriented when schedules shift, travel changes, or urgent demands collide.</li>\n<li><strong>Discreet by default.</strong> You handle highly confidential business and personal information with maturity, professionalism, and integrity.</li>\n</ul>\n<h1><strong>Minimum Qualifications</strong></h1>\n<ul>\n<li>3+ years of high-trust support experience with a founder, CEO, senior executive, high-profile individual, or similarly demanding principal, including 2+ years in a blended executive and personal assistant role.</li>\n<li>Demonstrated success managing complex calendars, competing demands, executive communications, personal coordination, and rapidly shifting priorities.</li>\n<li>Experience managing complex and multi-leg domestic and international travel.</li>\n<li>Exceptional organizational and project-management skills, with strong attention to detail across executive-level matters and hands-on personal requests.</li>\n<li>Strong business judgment, discretion, and the ability to assess urgency, make thoughtful tradeoffs, and act with minimal direction.</li>\n<li>Polished written and verbal communication skills, emotional intelligence, and the ability to build trust with senior internal and external stakeholders.</li>\n<li>Ability to work out of the San Francisco &amp; Palo Alto office 5 days per week, support irregular hours when necessary, and travel domestically and internationally based on business needs.</li>\n</ul>\n<h1><strong>Preferred Qualifications</strong></h1>\n<ul>\n<li>7+ years of experience supporting a founder, CEO, senior executive, entrepreneur, high-profile individual, or private office.</li>\n<li>Experience supporting a principal in technology, finance, luxury hospitality, travel, a family or private office, or another high-intensity environment.</li>\n<li>Experience coordinating executive and personal priorities across household staff, vendors, service providers, and external stakeholders.</li>\n<li>Bachelor\u2019s degree or equivalent professional experience.</li>\n</ul>\n<h1><strong>Before You Apply</strong></h1>\n<p>This role operates at the pace of the Founder &amp; CEO. Business and personal demands will not always occur during standard working hours, and travel or other priorities may change with little notice.</p>\n<p>This is not a traditional 9-to-5 position. It requires flexibility, discretion, and hands-on ownership across executive and personal support. If you are seeking a predictable schedule or a role limited to conventional administrative responsibilities, this may not be the right opportunity.</p>\n<h1><strong>Location &amp; Work Model</strong></h1>\n<ul>\n<li>Full-time, in-office role with time in both our Palo Alto and San Francisco offices and the flexibility to support the CEO wherever business requires.</li>\n<li>Flexibility to support priorities outside standard working hours when necessary</li>\n<li>Potential domestic and international travel based on business needs</li>\n</ul>\n<h1><strong>Compensation &amp; Benefits&nbsp;</strong></h1>\n<p class=\"isSelectedEnd\">The annual base salary range for this full-time position is <strong>$180,000\u2013$200,000 USD</strong>. In addition to base salary, this role is eligible for equity and benefits.</p>\n<p>Individual compensation will be determined based on job-related skills, experience, qualifications, and other relevant business considerations.</p>\n<h1><strong>Application Process</strong></h1>\n<p>Please submit:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Resume</li>\n<li>Professional references from a founder, CEO, senior executive, or high-profile individual you have directly supported</li>\n</ul