      "description": "<div class=\"content-intro\"><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(22, 145, 121);\"><strong>Netradyne</strong></span> harnesses the power of Computer Vision and Edge Computing to revolutionize the modern-day transportation ecosystem. We are a leader in fleet safety solutions. With growth exceeding 4x year over year, our solution is quickly being recognized as a significant disruptive technology. Our team is growing, and we need forward-thinking, uncompromising, competitive team members to continue to facilitate our growth.</p></div><p><strong><u>POSITION SUMMARY:</u></strong></p>\n<p>Netradyne is looking for a motivated individual to join our Product Management team as an Integrations Product Manager. This person will define integration requirements with partners/customers/resellers and enhance the product value to relevant stakeholders. They will conduct business analysis and lead scope preparation; understand technical requirements; interact with customers and vendors; collaborate in the development of training and materials for other departments and support these departments when promoting and selling integration services. The ideal candidate will be highly detail-oriented; self-starter, diligently organized, with excellent communication skills, and has a passion for excellence and values education, integrity, innovation, and success.</p>\n<p><strong><u>ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Define the integration scope of Netradyne systems/data with other software tools, such as a trucking fleet\u2019s ELD or routing systems, or others \u2013 with the goal of enhancing value for all stakeholders.</li>\n<li>Contribute to the integrations product roadmap from gathering customer feedback, writing PRDs, and collaborating with necessary teams to develop, test, and launch the integrations.</li>\n<li>Establish relationships with the Netradyne team, customers, and vendors, as needed, to effectively build out a comprehensive integration platform.</li>\n<li>Where appropriate, do minor scripting, querying, or validation to support the technical requirements.</li>\n<li>Learning and understanding the Netradyne web application functionality.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>QUALIFICATIONS:</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>Required:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>3+ years' experience as a Technical Product Manager and/or Program Manager.</li>\n<li>Bachelor's degree required, or equivalent experience.</li>\n<li>Knowledge of how to build API platforms and other integrations, preferably on a large scale.</li>\n<li>Experience with public Cloud and SaaS systems.</li>\n<li>Experience with technical integration technologies such as API/Webhook operations, SDK/APK concepts, as well as other web and database technology.</li>\n<li>Familiarity with AWS, Android, and IOS, as well as security concepts such as OAuth2 SSO protocols.</li>\n<li>An ability to analyze and find issues or bugs and work with the operations team to resolve them.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Preferred:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Experience with vehicle data/telematics is a plus.</li>\n<li>Excellent communication skills (verbal and written).</li>\n<li>Team player</li>\n<li>Self-motivated</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>EDUCATION:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Bachelor's degree required</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>*Hybrid Work Schedule:</u></strong></p>\n<p>We believe in the value of in-person collaboration while maintaining flexibility. Team members work from the office on&nbsp;<strong>Monday, Wednesday, and Thursday</strong>, with remote work on&nbsp;<strong>Tuesday and Friday</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>Economic Package Includes:</strong>&nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li><span data-teams=\"true\">Competitive Salary + eligibility for yearly bonus. The expected base pay range for this position is: Bay Area California $125,000-167,500, for Southern California $107,000-143,000&nbsp;</span></li>\n<li>Company equity</li>\n<li>Company Paid Health Care, Dental, and Vision Coverage for you and most of your dependents</li>\n<li>Generous PTO and Sick Leave</li>\n<li>401(K) with generous company match</li>\n<li>Disability, Life Insurance and Ancillary Benefits</li>\n<li>And much more</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p><div class=\"content-pay-transparency\"><div class=\"pay-input\"><div class=\"title\">San Diego Pay Range</div><div class=\"pay-range\"><span>$107,000</span><span class=\"divider\">&mdash;</span><span>$167,500 USD</span></div></div></div><div class=\"content-conclusion\"><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">We are committed to an inclusive and diverse team. Netradyne is an equal-opportunity employer. We do not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry, national origin, religion, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, age, disability, veteran status, genetic information, marital status, or any legally protected status.</p>\n<p>If there is a match between your experiences/skills and the Company's needs, we will contact you directly.</p>\n<p>Netradyne is an equal-opportunity employer.</p>\n<p><strong>Applicants only - Recruiting agencies do not contact.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Recruitment Fraud Alert!</strong></p>\n<p>There has been an increase in fraud that targets job seekers. Scammers may present themselves to job seekers as Netradyne employees or recruiters. Please be aware that Netradyne does not request sensitive personal data from applicants via text/instant message or any unsecured method; does not promise any advance payment for work equipment set-up and does not use recruitment or job-sourcing agencies that charge candidates an advance fee of any kind. Official communication about your application will only come from emails ending in \u2018@netradyne.com\u2019 or \u2018@us-greenhouse-mail.io\u2019.</p>\n<p>Please review and apply to our available job openings at Netradyne.com/company/careers. For more information on avoiding and reporting scams, please visit the <a href=\"https://consumer.ftc.gov/articles/job-scams\">Federal Trade Commission's job scams website</a>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p></div>",
