      "url": "https://jobs.lever.co/hevodata/3c22a84f-7eb6-4105-aa3b-7698322a98af",
      "description": "About Hevo\n\u00a0\nHevo moves data for more than 2,000 companies, including IcelandAir, Shopify, Postman, ThoughtSpot. What looks simple on the surface sits on top of some of the most complex machinery in software: pipelines pulling from 150+ sources, running every hour of every day, failing in a hundred different ways and recovering before anyone notices.\n\u00a0\nYour job is to make all of that feel obvious.\n\u00a0\nThis is one of the harder product design jobs going in India right now, and we want you to know that upfront. You are not designing a three-screen consumer app or a marketing site. You are designing for data engineers and analysts. They are technical, they are in a hurry, and they have no patience for design that gets in their way. If a workflow confuses them, they do not \"figure it out.\" They leave. Good design here is not decoration. It is the product.\n\u00a0\nOne more thing before you read further: this role is AI-first, and we mean it as a requirement, not a bonus. We explain exactly what that means below. Please read it closely.\n\n\nWhat you will own:\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">The experience of complex workflows.</span></strong><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"> You will own the UX for the hard, high-stakes parts of the product end to end, from research and problem framing to the final shipped screen. Large scope, real ambiguity, technical users.</span></p>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">The full design process, not a slice of it.</span></strong><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"> User journeys, wireframes, prototypes, high-fidelity mockups. You take a fuzzy problem and turn it into something people can actually use, then you stand in front of product, engineering, and customers and explain why you made the calls you made.</span></p>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">The design system.</span></strong><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"> You will extend and strengthen the system that keeps the Hevo dashboard feeling like one product instead of ten. Consistency at our scale is a real, engineering-grade problem, not a coat of paint.</span></p>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Shipping, measured.</span></strong><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"> You will watch how people actually use what you built, read the data honestly, and change your mind when the numbers tell you to. Designers who fall in love with their first idea do not do well here.</span></p>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">The bar for the whole team.</span></strong><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"> You will push product and engineering to care about the details most teams skip: accessibility, edge cases, the unglamorous states. Seniority here means raising everyone's standard, not just doing your own work well.</span></p>\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\nWhat \"AI-first\" means here:\n<div>\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">We mean two things, and we need both.</span></p>\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\">&nbsp;</p>\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">One: you design AI-native products, not old screens with an AI button bolted on.</span></strong><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"> The best software today is being rebuilt around what AI can now do: agents, generation, suggestions, systems that act on a user's behalf. These experiences behave differently from the deterministic screens most of us grew up designing. They are probabilistic. They are wrong sometimes. They need new patterns for trust, control, and letting a user correct the machine. You should have real opinions on how to design for this, and ideally, work that shows it.</span></p>\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Two: AI is part of your daily craft.</span></strong><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"> You use it to research faster, generate directions, write product copy, and build working prototypes in hours instead of weeks. You are not precious about doing everything by hand. The strongest designers we are meeting today treat AI like the sharpest junior on their team and direct it well. That is the bar we are hiring against.</span></p>\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">If you are curious about AI but have not actually shipped with it, this role will be a stretch, and we would rather say that now than waste your time.<br></span></p>\n</div>\n\nWho you are:\n<div>\n<ul style=\"margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; padding-inline-start: 48px;\">\n<li style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\">4 to 8 years</span></strong><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\"> designing and shipping real products inside a cross-functional team. In-house, not agency-only.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\">SaaS background.</span></strong><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\"> You have designed software that businesses pay for and rely on every day. This is a requirement.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\">Web app design experience.</span></strong><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\"> You have designed complex, interactive web applications, not just websites, mobile screens, or brand work. This is a requirement.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\">AI-first</span></strong><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\">, in both senses above. This is a requirement.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\">Strong UX for technical or enterprise products.</span></strong><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\"> You are comfortable when the subject matter is hard and the users know more than you do.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\">A portfolio that shows your thinking</span></strong><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\">, not just your pixels. We want to see the problem, the messy middle, the decisions you made, and the result.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\">Fluent in the tools</span></strong><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\">, Figma above all, plus whatever helps you prototype and test quickly.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\">A strong communicator.</span></strong><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\"> You can explain a design decision to an engineer, a PM, and a customer, and win each of them over on the merits.</span></p>\n</li>\n\n</ul></div>",
